// In-body links ADDED after the WordPress export, so a newly published article
// is reachable from the pages that already rank for its topic.
//
// lib/recovered-internal-links.ts records what the deployed site carried and is
// regenerated by a script, so it must not be hand-edited. This file sits beside
// it: the entries here are merged in front of a page's recovered list, which is
// otherwise a closed set (a page with a recovered list gets those links and
// nothing else — so without this table a new article can only be reached from
// /blog/ and the hub grids).
//
// Shape is the same as INJECTED_LINKS: [anchor phrase, target path, paragraph].
// The third item is the start of the paragraph the link belongs in, matched
// against the paragraph's visible text; it keeps the anchor on the sentence
// that is actually about the target rather than the first mention on the page.
// The anchor phrase itself must also be a literal substring of THAT paragraph
// — linkifyInternal searches for it inside the matched paragraph only, not
// across the whole page.

